## S1 — Import name zero-trust (`reject_bad_import_name`)
### Source
`ooda/oodac/load_import.oo` L93–124:

- empty → `ERR\timport\tempty name` + `process_exit(1)`
- leading `/` → absolute path rejected
- leading `~` → home path rejected
- contains `..` → path escape rejected
- contains `\` → backslash rejected
- any NUL char → NUL rejected

Call site L167–169: after `parse_import_line`, non-empty names always hit
`reject_bad_import_name` before `path_join` / `load_expand`.

### Live product-host matrix (`oodac check`, RC=1 unless noted)
| Attack | Import name | Result | RC |
|--------|-------------|--------|-----|
| absolute | `/etc/passwd` | `ERR import absolute path rejected` | 1 |
| home | `~/evil.oo` | `ERR import home path rejected` | 1 |
| parent | `../etc/passwd` | `ERR import path escape rejected` | 1 |
| nested `..` | `a/../../etc/passwd` | path escape rejected | 1 |
| deep `..` | `foo/../../../tmp/x` | path escape rejected | 1 |
| backslash | `foo\bar.oo` | backslash path rejected | 1 |
| dblslash abs | `//etc/passwd` | absolute path rejected | 1 |
| missing | `no_such_mod.oo` | not found after relative probes | 1 |
| cycle | a↔b | `ERR import cycle involving …` | 1 |
| OK relative | `ok_mod.oo` | `OK` | 0 |
| empty `import ""` | (parse returns non-import) | `OK` | 0 — residual |
| NUL in name | real `\0` mid-string | truncated to `ab.oo` → not found (RC=1) — residual vs explicit NUL msg |
| percent-encode | `%2e%2e/etc/passwd` | not found (no decode) | 1 |
| fullwidth dots | `．．/x.oo` | not found | 1 |

Binary strings present: absolute / home / path escape / backslash / NUL /
relative probes (product host).

**Verdict S1: PASS** for the named zero-trust rejects that reach the
validator. Residuals: empty-string parse skip; NUL may truncate before
explicit NUL branch (still fail-closed).

